                <pb facs="0141" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7661/16.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-16"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 16,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson states that in reference to his cable of September 10, Underwood’s
                    deviled ham, new analysis, shows no boric acid. Also states that ham at
                    custom-house will be admitted and that all future shipments will be admitted
                    subject to occasional analysis.)</p>
            </div>
